{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>The Festival of Unleavened Bread.</b> Begin with it, for it is first among the months of the year. Now it is written: \"seven days you shall eat unleavened bread,\" like \"the Festival of Booths you shall make for yourself seven days\" (Deuteronomy 16:13). This is an obligation, and there is none like it — \"six days you shall do your work\" (below, v. 12) — for after it is written that you shall rest on the seventh day, but it is not so with \"seven days you shall eat unleavened bread.\" And further, why is it not written: \"seven days you shall not eat leavened bread\"?" "<b>The month of Aviv.</b> I have explained it." "Many thought that \"they shall not appear before Me empty\" is like \"and My face shall not be seen\" (below 33:23). This is not correct, for those who come to the House of HaShem are seen, and the proof is \"and we will appear before the face of YHWH\" (1 Samuel 1:22), and also \"every male of yours shall appear before the face of HaShem\" (Deuteronomy 16:16) — like \"before HaShem.\""], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:42.859359794Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}